.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-GRANT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-grant - Set or revoke an explicit resource permission


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team grant <team> <account> <env|preview|tunnel> <resource> <permission> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set or revoke an explicit resource permission

.PP
Set or revoke an explicit ENV, preview, or tunnel permission for one account and resource. --active selects grant state, and --generation rejects stale team edits.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant device use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--active\fP[=true]
	grant permission; set false to revoke

.PP
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for grant

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
